1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Water dripping from your headliner
after it rains?

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:04,900
Might not be a roof leak.

3
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:09,000
Most sunroofs have four drain tubes
that carry rainwater through the pillars.

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Leaves and dirt can clog one,
so water backs up instead of draining out.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,000
That backup finds the easiest way in —
usually the headliner or a rear pillar.

6
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:24,000
One clue: it usually only happens
after rain or a car wash — not all the time.

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Worth checking before you assume
it's a full roof leak.

8
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Stop by and we'll take a look.
